nix-eh
======

Put the useful part of a Nix error first, with the original output still available.

Run
---

From this complete source folder on a Nix host:

   nix run path:. -- read /tmp/nix-error.log
   nix run path:. -- --full read /tmp/nix-error.log
   nix run path:. -- --json read /tmp/nix-error.log
   nix run path:. -- run -- nix build --show-trace

Nix provides Python automatically. Enable nix-command and flakes, or pass
--extra-experimental-features "nix-command flakes" to Nix. A first run may
fetch or build dependencies. Keep the complete source folder and lock files together.

Read or wrap a command
----------------------

* read FILE: Format a saved log; read - accepts stdin
* run -- COMMAND ...: Preserve command arguments, stdin, stdout and exit
  status; format stderr after completion
* --full: Include original diagnostics after the summary
* --json: Return structured diagnostics, including original text

Put global options before the subcommand. In run mode, JSON goes to stderr
so stdout remains usable. Successful read formatting returns zero even when
the log describes a failure; use your shell's pipefail when the producer's
exit status matters.

Insecure-package summaries show the blocked package and stated issues. Trace
references are investigation hints, not proof of which application caused the
problem. No override or repair is run automatically.

Limits and checks
-----------------

The final reported error can be a downstream symptom. Suggestions and source
locations need review; diagnostics can contain private paths or values. Keep
saved output outside this source folder and inspect it before sharing.

Explicit run buffers stderr, which can delay progress and interactive prompts.
Run interactive commands directly and format their saved logs instead. Native
Nix builds, activation and terminal behaviour are not established by fixture tests.

Run source regression checks with python3 -B -m unittest -v.
On a Nix host, nix flake check path:. runs the configured package checks.
